+ ### Response Shape (All Methods)
+ Every CellCog SDK method returns the same shape:
+ {
+     "chat_id": str,        # CellCog chat ID
+     "is_operating": bool,  # True = still working, False = done
+     "status": str,         # "completed" | "tracking" | "timeout" | "operating"
+     "message": str,        # THE printable message — always print this in full
+ }
+ **⚠️ Always print the entire `result["message"]`.** CellCog output comes from an AI agent and can be lengthy. Truncating or summarizing it will lose critical information including generated file paths, credits used, and follow-up instructions.
+ result = client.create_chat(prompt="...", task_label="...")
+ print(result["message"])  # Print the full response
+ ### get_history()
+ Retrieve full chat history. Use when the original delivery was missed, truncated, or you need to review a previous chat:
+ result = client.get_history(chat_id="abc123")
+ print(result["message"])  # Full history with all messages and files
+ Returns the same `{chat_id, is_operating, status, message}` shape. If the chat is still operating, `message` shows progress so far.
+ Quick status check (lightweight, no history fetch):
+ client.send_message(chat_id="abc123", message="Actually focus only on Q4 data")
+ client.send_message(chat_id="abc123", message="Stop operation")
